From 6e3b4af97495528e9a838444ea5008b0e5b013f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:59:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: give M4 userspace queues independent firmware
 queues

Keep descriptors, rings, event leases and stamp sequences per public queue, retained through in-flight completion. Use the matching fragment event for partial restart and the M1/M2 non-preempting compute profile with private Work scratch.

Validate eight compute/render queues, partial rendering, concurrent Mesa clients, pending teardown, mixed batches, delayed fences, timestamps and local indirect compute on M4 hardware.

(cherry picked from commit 680d7f44383fdd422827d83284e467f4ea112cb6)
